surname>Mak</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowe</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Conn</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lu</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Cox</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk of influenza A (H5N1) infection among poultry workers, Hong Kong, 1997&#x02013;1998</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source><year>2002</year><volume>185</volume><fpage>1005</fpage><lpage>1010</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11930308</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/340044</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alexander</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Schudel A, Lombard M</surname></name></person-group><source>Avian influenza viruses and human health</source><year>2006</year><volume>124</volume><publisher-name>Developments in Biologicals Karger, Switzerland</publisher-name><fpage>77</fpage><lpage>84</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16447497</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Perez</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Seiler</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Yi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Peiris</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Shortridge</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of Quail in the interspecies transmission of H9 influenza A viruses: molec